file pond/enclosure_policy.rye the env mark joins Kind, kind_name, kind_for_token and the dispatch; verdict_for_env_key and verdict_for_env added; run_check reads one byte past the bound so PolicyTooLong is reachable; nineteen selftest assertions
file pond/enclosure_policy.kyri two env lines declaring what the exec line spells, a trimmed header naming the .gh finding and the byte pressure
file tools/fixtures/p/pond_enclosure_door_scan.sh the env declaration lifted and settled against the exec line; env_disagreements gated at zero; duties_undeclared falls to 1
file tools/fixtures/p/pond_enclosure_door_control.sh five new pens, fourteen new assertions, and the elder space-spelled env line repaired to the seated grammar
file tools/p/pond_enclosure_door_witness.rish the duty pin moves 2 to 1, the new readings assert, and the env settling is proven from the refusing side without a kernel
file tools/fixtures/p/pond_enclosure_policy_scan.sh an ENV leg at the terminal door and a TOOLONG leg proving the bound from both sides on real files
file tools/w/waymark_rung_drift_witness.rish two nested absolute interpreter spellings take the PATH-resolved form, with the vacuous pass named above the pen block
file construction/REDS.md rows 20260830.031001 and 20260830.032600 booked and closed; headline re-measured
file construction/archive/REDS-the-fleet-catches-itself-rows-345-349.md the shelf, with a header naming what the five rows share
file construction/archive/REDS-fold-recital.md the fold recorded, which returns unrecorded_shelves to its ceiling
file construction/ITINERARY.md Now re-aimed at the door, Pond live at one duty, both reds and the fold named, and the card trimmed back under 24,576
recommend check-in (Keaton) -- POND'S RECORD CAN NOW SAY WHAT CROSSES ITS DOOR, and the one duty left is a gate rather than a lap. `env` seats as KEY=value in the exec line's own spelling, its value half read as a search path so one rule serves a directory and a four-element PATH alike; the door guard settles it against the launcher at env_disagreements ZERO ENFORCED and proves that refusal WITHOUT a kernel, which is what makes it a gate on every pier rather than only on this one. duties_undeclared falls 2 to 1. THE LAST DUTY IS `entry`, AND SEATING IT IS THE SWITCHOVER -- naming the program inside the record is the moment Pond stops describing an enclosure somebody else builds, so orbit four's remainder is your word rather than my next lap. TWO REDS FELL OUT OF THE SEATING, both closed on metal. The first was mine to take at the roster: %353's interpreter sweep had left two spellings nested inside a `bash -c` string in the very file it repaired, where exit 127 satisfied `bitten.ok == false` and a refusing-side proof was passing vacuously -- a refusal must refuse, and it must refuse for its OWN reason. The second no guard caught: my own header pushed the record past max_policy_len, and a read buffer sized AT the bound made that bound's own check unreachable by construction, so the checker judged 31 declarations of 34 and counted a half-line as a refusal of a line that does not exist. Arithmetic on the receipt found it. THE PIN FOLDED TO HOLD THEM -- 408 bytes of headroom against a 2,400-byte row, so rows went to their own shelf through reds_fold.sh with the recital recorded. ONE THING I DECLINED: pond/enclosure_policy.kyri stands at 8,120 of 8,192 and nearly all of it is the comment that makes the record auditable, so `entry`'s own paragraph meets that wall. Whether the bound should read declarations rather than the whole document is a real question, and %347 says widening one takes your word -- so I trimmed my own prose to cite rather than restate and left the question with you. MINE NEXT, AND SILENCE HANDED IT ACROSS: its `%354` reads OPEN with the Tablecloth half repaired and the `spool_cloth` twin named for me -- `pond/apps/spool_cloth.rye` carries the same separator hole, and `pond/apps/tablecloth.rye` holds the shape to copy. I take it with %341's four-against-two in one sitting, since both live in that one file. ONE MORE THING FROM THE SEND: xy had moved, and Silence's %354 was booked four minutes ahead of mine, so my two rows shifted to `%355` and `%356` keeping their stamps -- the derived-spine law's seventh firing and the first that needed no diagnosis. The collision also reshaped my fold from %345-%349 to %347-%349, which made its header truer: those three were each found by a body that could not have made the repair, where %345 and %346 were you reading pushed commits.
